          %p
            Consequently, in a category with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+object"} exponentiable object
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo !
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !_X : X \to 1
            is an exponentiable morphism.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has equalizers of coreflexive pairs, then any pullback of an exponentiable morphism is exponentiable. This follows from the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triangle+theorem"} adjoint triangle theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_f
              of pullback is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonadic+functor"} comonadic
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conduche+functor"} Exponentiable functors
                are characterised by a factorisation property.
            %li
              %p
                The exponentiable morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                were characterized by
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Niefield82"} Niefield
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to D
                is exponentiable if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    locally closed
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/locally+closed"} ?
            %li
              %p
                The exponentiable morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Locale
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Locale
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Topos
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
                which are embeddings were also characterized by
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Niefield81"} Niefield
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Locale
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Locale
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Topos
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
                appears in the literature.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A category is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed"} locally cartesian closed
                precisely when it has all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                and in which every morphism is exponentiable.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_f
                is described by a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+pullback"} distributivity pullback
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                exist.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theoretic
                interpretation of exponential morphisms is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+object"} exponentiable object
          %h2#references References
          %ul
